---
// FXR-239 (Kanvas v7): neues Gerüst, KEIN geänderter Text.
import TextPage from '../layouts/TextPage.astro';
---
<TextPage
  title="FAQ"
  description="Frequently asked questions about FixedR: prop-only policy, MetaTrader and NinjaTrader support, local-first data, R-only display."
  eyebrow="Questions, answered plainly"
  h1="FAQ"
  seite="FAQ"
  hinweis="Eight questions. If yours isn't here, it belongs on the waitlist form."
>
  <div class="faq-liste">
    <details class="eintrag" open>
      <summary><span class="frage">Why is FixedR only for prop-firm accounts?</span><span class="pfeil"><svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 10 10" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"><path d="M2 3.5l3 3 3-3"></path></svg></span></summary>
      <div class="antwort">
        <p>
          By design and by policy. FixedR carries out the order you place on several accounts at
          once, and software that touches orders must never be in a position to damage someone's
          private savings through a defect. Funded
          accounts are the right habitat: the firm's capital, clearly bounded rules, and a
          risk-first mindset already required by the challenge. FixedR is not made for private
          accounts.
        </p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="eintrag">
      <summary><span class="frage">Which platforms does it work with?</span><span class="pfeil"><svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 10 10" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"><path d="M2 3.5l3 3 3-3"></path></svg></span></summary>
      <div class="antwort">
        <p>
          MetaTrader and NinjaTrader. FixedR sits beside your platform as the cockpit — placing,
          sizing and journaling — while the platform remains the execution venue.
        </p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="eintrag">
      <summary><span class="frage">Really no money display at all? Not even an option?</span><span class="pfeil"><svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 10 10" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"><path d="M2 3.5l3 3 3-3"></path></svg></span></summary>
      <div class="antwort">
        <p>
          Really. There is no money mode and no hidden toggle. The absence is deliberate: an option
          you can switch on in a weak moment is not a commitment device. The only exception is the
          account size you enter once when connecting an account — after that, everything is R.
        </p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="eintrag">
      <summary><span class="frage">Where does my data live?</span><span class="pfeil"><svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 10 10" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"><path d="M2 3.5l3 3 3-3"></path></svg></span></summary>
      <div class="antwort">
        <p>
          On your machine. FixedR is a local-first Windows application: your journal, account
          configuration and trading records are stored in a local database and are not sent to us.
          You do have a FixedR account: an e-mail address and a password, used to sign in and to
          check your licence, and that needs an internet connection. The full list of what
          crosses the line is on <a href="/trust">Trust</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="eintrag">
      <summary><span class="frage">Does this website track me?</span><span class="pfeil"><svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 10 10" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"><path d="M2 3.5l3 3 3-3"></path></svg></span></summary>
      <div class="antwort">
        {/* E-C161: der Anspruch endet an der Mess-Grenze. „Diese Seite trackt dich nicht"
            wäre in dem Moment falsch, in dem ein Kampagnen-Link eine Quelle unterscheidet.
            Also: keine FREMD-Tracker, kein Datenverkauf — und offen sagen, was gemessen wird. */}
        <p>
          No third-party trackers, no advertising pixels, no cookies, no external fonts or scripts.
          Nothing about you is sold or shared. What we do count is how many people join the waitlist
          and which link they arrived from — a number, not a profile. The waitlist form is the only
          thing that sends data anywhere, and only what you type into it.
        </p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="eintrag">
      <summary><span class="frage">What does R mean, exactly?</span><span class="pfeil"><svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 10 10" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"><path d="M2 3.5l3 3 3-3"></path></svg></span></summary>
      <div class="antwort">
        <p>
          R is the amount you decided to risk on a trade, fixed by your stop before entry. A trade
          that hits its stop is <span class="r-value">-1R</span>. A trade closed at twice the risked
          amount is <span class="r-value">+2R</span>. Because R is defined relative to your own
          risk, results stay comparable across instruments, account sizes and time.
        </p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="eintrag">
      <summary><span class="frage">Will FixedR help me pass my evaluation?</span><span class="pfeil"><svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 10 10" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"><path d="M2 3.5l3 3 3-3"></path></svg></span></summary>
      <div class="antwort">
        <p>
          No tool can promise that, and you should distrust any that does. What FixedR does is
          structural: it makes the disciplined path the only path the software offers — mandatory
          stops, fixed risk, no money number to tilt against. The trading is still yours.
        </p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="eintrag">
      <summary><span class="frage">When can I get it? What does it cost?</span><span class="pfeil"><svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 10 10" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"><path d="M2 3.5l3 3 3-3"></path></svg></span></summary>
      <div class="antwort">
        <p>
          FixedR is currently in a closed founders phase with a small group of prop traders.
          Prices are not final. What is decided is the cut: every plan has every feature, and plans
          differ only in how many accounts you trade at once. The base price on the
          <a href="/#pricing">home page</a> is a proposal, and the higher plans have no price yet.
          Founders get a reduced price for a limited time, and it is stated in the invitation. The
          <a href="/waitlist">waitlist</a> is the way in — founders-circle invitations go out in
          order of signup.
        </p>
      </div>
    </details>
    <span class="schluss"></span>
  </div>
</TextPage>
